You'll plan the work for

259
00:10:39,160 --> 00:10:40,765
the next sprint and
the previous sprint.

260
00:10:40,765 --> 00:10:43,074
As I mentioned with the
final project proposal,

261
00:10:43,074 --> 00:10:45,640
you'll be proposing what
you do in Sprint 1.

262
00:10:45,640 --> 00:10:47,515
When you complete Sprint 1,

263
00:10:47,515 --> 00:10:51,130
you'll propose what you do
for Sprint 2, and so on.

264
00:10:51,130 --> 00:10:53,140
You'll use the GitHub
issues that I showed

265
00:10:53,140 --> 00:10:55,210
previously to track
and report your work

266
00:10:55,210 --> 00:10:57,790
and you'll use
GitHub Wiki pages to

267
00:10:57,790 --> 00:10:59,500
report on the overall progress

268
00:10:59,500 --> 00:11:01,700
and status of your project.

269
00:11:01,730 --> 00:11:04,860
The general schedule
for the project looks

270
00:11:04,860 --> 00:11:06,630
like this final project proposal

271
00:11:06,630 --> 00:11:07,875
that I'm talking about now,

272
00:11:07,875 --> 00:11:10,135
the first week, then Sprint 1,

273
00:11:10,135 --> 00:11:14,260
Sprint 2, and Sprint 3 in
consecutive weeks or blocks

274
00:11:14,260 --> 00:11:16,150
of time depending on
whether you're taking

275
00:11:16,150 --> 00:11:18,950
this course synchronously
or asynchronously.

276
00:11:18,950 --> 00:11:22,875
You'll also complete
the final project

277
00:11:22,875 --> 00:11:25,815
with a demo outline
and video detailing

278
00:11:25,815 --> 00:11:28,770
your individual contribution
to the project and

